  constructor(camera: Camera) {
    this.camera = camera;
  }

  public animate(duration: number, easingFunction?: (t: number) => number): void {
    // Implement animation logic here
  }
}

const camera = new Camera();
const animationAPI = new AnimationAPI(camera);

animationAPI.animate(1000, (t) => t * t); // Ease-in quadratic easing
```

This API provides a simple `animate` method that takes a duration and an optional easing function as parameters. The `Camera` class is responsible for handling the camera logic, such as position, rotation, and field of view.

You can customize the `animate` method to implement different animation techniques, such as keyframe animations, particle systems, or physics-based animations.

To use this API, you would first create a `Camera` instance and then pass it to the `AnimationAPI` constructor. You can then call the `animate` method to start the animation.

