To use the updateAAD method in the AEAD GCM cipher class for authentication, you can follow these steps:

1. Import the necessary classes:
```java
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.spec.GCMParameterSpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
```
2. Create a secret key and initialize the cipher with it:
```java
String secretKey = "your_secret_key";
byte[] secretKeyBytes = secretKey.getBytes();
SecretKeySpec secretKeySpec = new SecretKeySpec(secretKeyBytes, "AES");
Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, secretKeySpec);
```
3. Use the updateAAD method to authenticate data:
```java
byte[] data = "your_data_to_authenticate".getBytes();
byte[] tag = cipher.doFinal(data);
```
4. Verify the authenticity of data using the updateAAD method:
```java
byte[] receivedData = "received_data_to_verify".getBytes();
byte[] receivedTag = cipher.doFinal(receivedData);
if (Arrays.equals(tag, receivedTag)) {
    System.out.println("Data is authentic.");
} else {
    System.out.println("Data is not authentic.");
}
```
Note that the updateAAD method is used to authenticate data using the Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data (AEAD) GCM cipher. This method ensures that the data is both encrypted and authenticated, providing a secure way to transmit sensitive information.

