To fix this issue, you can add the following code snippet to your theme's functions.php file or a site-specific plugin:

```php
add_filter( 'wpseo_opengraph_description', '__return_false' );
add_filter( 'wpseo_opengraph_image_url', '__return_false' );
add_filter( 'wpseo_opengraph_site_name', '__return_false' );
add_filter( 'wpseo_opengraph_title', '__return_false' );
add_filter( 'wpseo_opengraph_type', '__return_false' );
add_filter( 'wpseo_opengraph_url', '__return_false' );
```

This will disable Yoast SEO's Open Graph meta tags, which might be causing the issue with Facebook not detecting the image. However, keep in mind that disabling these meta tags may affect how your content appears when shared on social media platforms.

To fix this issue, you need to add an Open Graph meta tag for the image in your WordPress blog post. You can do this by adding the following code to your theme's `functions.php` file or a site-specific plugin:

```php
function add_open_graph_meta() {
    $image_url = get_the_post_thumbnail_url();
    if ($image_url) {
        echo '<meta property="og:image" content="' . $image_url . '">';
    }
}
add_action('wp_head', 'add_open_graph_meta');
```

This code will add an Open Graph meta tag for the featured image of your blog post. If you don't have a featured image set, you can use the `get_the_post_thumbnail_url()` function to get the first image in the post and use that as the Open Graph image.

Alternatively, you can use a plugin like "Yoast SEO" which has an option to add Open Graph meta tags to your blog posts. Simply install and activate the plugin, then go to the "Social" tab in the Yoast SEO settings and enable the "Open Graph" feature. From there, you can select the image you want to use as the Open Graph image for your blog post.

Once you've added the Open Graph meta tag, you should see the image displayed when you share your blog post on Facebook.

```javascript
function postSlackMessage(text, channel) {
  // Replace with your Slack API credentials
  const token = 'your_token_here';
  const webhookUrl = `https://hooks.slack.com/services/${channel}/${token}`;

  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      text: text
    })
  });
}
```

```javascript
function postSlackMessage(text, channel) {
    // Replace these values with your actual Slack API credentials
    const token = 'your_token';
    const webhookUrl = `https://hooks.slack.com/services/${channel}/${token}`;

    fetch(webhookUrl, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
            'Content-Type': 'application/json'
        },
        body: JSON.stringify({
            text: text
        })
    });
