The `app.useGlobalGuards()` method is used to register the `PermissionGuard` as a global guard for the application. This means that all requests to the application will be subject to the permission guard's authorization checks.

The `dbOptions` object configures the connection to the MySQL database. The `entities` property specifies the directory where the entity classes are located. The `synchronize` property sets the synchronization mode for the database schema.

Finally, the `export default app` statement exports the application instance so that it can be imported and used in other parts of the application.

To create an Apps Script that searches for a place name in a column and stores the latitude and longitude in other columns, follow these steps:

1. Open Google Sheets and enable the Apps Script editor by clicking "Extensions" > "Apps Script."
2. In the Apps Script editor, create a new function called `searchPlace` with the following code:
```javascript
function searchPlace(sheetName, columnA, columnB, columnC) {
  var sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet().getSheetByName(sheetName);
  var dataRange = sheet.getRange(2, columnA, sheet.getLastRow() - 1, 1);
  var values = dataRange.getValues();

  for (var i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
    var place = values[i][0];
    var latLongUrl = "https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?address=" + encodeURIComponent(place) + "&key=YOUR_API_KEY";

    var response = UrlFetchApp.fetch(latLongUrl);
    var json = JSON.parse(response);

    if (json.results.length > 0) {
      var latitude = json.results[0].geometry.location.lat;
      var longitude = json.results[0].geometry.location.lng;

      sheet.getRange(i + 2, columnB).setValue(latitude);
      sheet.getRange(i + 2, columnC).setValue(longitude);
    } else {
      sheet.getRange(i + 2, columnB).setValue("");
      sheet.getRange(i + 2, columnC).setValue("");
    }
  }
}
```
Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Google Maps API key.
3. Call the `searchPlace` function from another function or trigger it using a button or schedule.
