to create a socket for chatroom, give me a example.

response:
Here's an example of how you can create a socket for chat rooms using your given database schema:

```php
<?php

// Database connection
$servername = "localhost";
$username = "username";
$password = "password";
$dbname = "database_name";

$conn = new mysqli($servername, $username, $password, $dbname);

if ($conn->connect_error) {
    die("Connection failed: " . $conn->connect_error);
}

// Socket server setup
$host = "0.0.0.0";
$port = 3000;

socket_create($sock, AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, $protocol);
socket_bind($sock, $host, $port);
socket_listen($sock);

// Accept incoming connections
while (true) {
    $newSocket = socket_accept($sock);
    if ($newSocket === false) {
        echo "Error accepting client: " . socket_strerror(socket_last_error()) . "\n";
        break;
    }

    // Handle incoming messages
    while (true) {
        $msg = socket_read($newSocket, 1024);
        if ($msg === false) {
            echo "Error reading from client: " . socket_strerror(socket_last_error()) . "\n";
            break;
        }

        // Process the message here (e.g., send to chat room)
        // ...

        // Send response to client
        socket_write($newSocket, "Received: " . $msg . "\n");
    }

    // Close the socket when the client disconnects
    socket_close($newSocket);
}

// Close the socket server
socket_close($sock);

// Close the database connection
$conn->close();

?>
```

This script sets up a simple socket server on port 3000 that accepts incoming connections and handles incoming messages. You can modify this script to suit your specific needs and integrate it with your existing database schema.

